{"id": "unknown-2026-10-13-006", "date": "2026-10-13", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "US power prices fall with utility-scale solar, rise with rooftop", "content": "<p>MIT researchers say there is no link between renewable portfolio standards or utility-scale wind and solar and higher US residential power prices, but rooftop solar correlates with higher rates and distribution costs.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/13/us-power-prices-fall-with-utility-scale-solar-rise-with-rooftop/\">US power prices fall with utility-scale solar, rise with rooftop</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.<", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/13/us-power-prices-fall-with-utility-scale-solar-rise-with-rooftop/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-13-007", "date": "2026-10-13", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Leapting launches autonomous forklift for solar module transport", "content": "<p>The Chinese robotics manufacturer has introduced an autonomous tracked forklift capable of transporting solar module pallets weighing up to 3,000 kg. The battery-powered machine features a maximum lifting height of 3 m, a 30-degree climbing capability and a navigation system combining GNSS-RTK, laser SLAM and computer vision.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/13/leapting-launches-autonomous-forklift-for-solar-module-transport/\">Leapting launches autonomous forklift ", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/13/leapting-launches-autonomous-forklift-for-solar-module-transport/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-13-008", "date": "2026-10-13", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Exide launches modular 125 kW/261 kWh battery for C&I applications", "content": "<p>The French manufacturer has introduced a new lithium iron phosphate (LFP) battery featuring an integrated 125 kW power conversion system, 261 kWh of storage capacity and a nominal round-trip efficiency of 86%.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/13/exide-launches-modular-125-kw-261-kwh-battery-for-ci-applications/\">Exide launches modular 125 kW/261 kWh battery for C&amp;I applications</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.<", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/13/exide-launches-modular-125-kw-261-kwh-battery-for-ci-applications/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-13-009", "date": "2026-10-13", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["improve"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Three-molecule blend boosts inverted perovskite solar cell efficiency to 27.5%", "content": "<p>Chinese researchers have developed high-entropy molecular contacts that enabled inverted perovskite solar cells to achieve a certified steady-state efficiency of 27.31%. The approach also improves thermal stability by preventing molecular contact degradation.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/13/three-molecule-blend-boosts-inverted-perovskite-solar-cell-efficiency-to-27-5/\">Three-molecule blend boosts inverted perovskite solar cell efficiency to 27.5%</a> appeared f", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/13/three-molecule-blend-boosts-inverted-perovskite-solar-cell-efficiency-to-27-5/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-13-010", "date": "2026-10-13", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Stationary, moving, flexible: Batteries are the low-cost backbone of the future energy system", "content": "<p>While it is known that batteries are indispensable for the future energy system dominated by solar PV, they are still seen as a bottleneck technology mostly related to raw material supply. Sodium-ion batteries can resolve this issue. Batteries are more than a stationary storage technology, also with bright prospects for vehicle-to-grid (V2G) and smart charging of electric vehicles within a broad flexibility technology portfolio.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/13/", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/13/stationary-moving-flexible-batteries-are-the-low-cost-backbone-of-the-future-energy-system/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-13-011", "date": "2026-10-13", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": ["record", "decline"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "European PPA prices rise 5% in September", "content": "<p>European PPA prices rose 5% in September, driven by higher forward electricity and gas prices, while Spain and Portugal recorded declines. Contracting activity rebounded, with 25 deals totaling 1.2 GW, alongside growing interest in hybrid PPAs and battery storage agreements.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/13/european-ppa-prices-rise-5-in-september/\">European PPA prices rise 5% in September</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Gl", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/13/european-ppa-prices-rise-5-in-september/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-13-012", "date": "2026-10-13", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["installation_demand", "industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Enpal, Würth unveil safety platform for PV deployment on pitched roofs", "content": "<p>The new RAST system combines roof access, fall protection and material transport in a standardized installation process. German trade associations BG ETEM and BG BAU supported its development. </p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/13/enpal-wurth-unveil-safety-platform-for-pv-deployment-on-pitched-roofs/\">Enpal, Würth unveil safety platform for PV deployment on pitched roofs</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/13/enpal-wurth-unveil-safety-platform-for-pv-deployment-on-pitched-roofs/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-13-013", "date": "2026-10-13", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 1.0, "keywords": ["leading"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "Qatar’s renewable capacity share could more than double by 2035", "content": "<p>Renewables could rise from 12% of Qatar's power capacity in 2025 to 25.9% by 2035, says GlobalData, with solar leading while gas remains the backbone of its power and water system.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/13/qatars-renewable-capacity-share-to-more-than-double-by-2035/\">Qatar&#8217;s renewable capacity share could more than double by 2035</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/13/qatars-renewable-capacity-share-to-more-than-double-by-2035/", "type": "rss"}]}
